<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Iraqi oil inspectors say plans on hold.</title>
<headline>Dutch Iraqi oil inspectors say plans on hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch industrial inspectors Saybolt said on Monday their plans to despatch 14 monitors to Iraq and Turkey had been temporarily suspended.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything is on hold for the time being. The situation is not clearly established. We have spoken to the U.N. and are awaiting further instructions from them,&quot; Peter Boks, manager of business development at Saybolt, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Boks said the situation may become clearer after Monday's Labor Day holiday in the U.S.</p>
</text>
